From 0052e8ac2ecb953b3a2f8a4bcd941b9f2fdb3c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:56:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(venue-base): injectable Safe broadcaster
 (createBaseVenue({ safeBroadcaster }))

A host whose service Safe is not owned by an EOA it holds a WalletClient for
(e.g. an ERC-4337 smart account with a hardware key, calling execTransaction
itself with a pre-validated v = 1 signature) passes a factory. The factory
receives the venue's own durable lock and submission ledger, so the
single-broadcaster rule holds for it as for the built-in EOA broadcaster.
walletClient becomes optional when a factory is given.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
